A change of ours to JUCE 9.0.4, macOS only. cmake/Dependencies.cmake applies it to the
downloaded sources through cmake/ApplyPatch.cmake, exactly or not at all, and the configure
stops when it no longer applies or the sources lack it.

Why: macOS asks the user for the microphone as soon as an IOProc is created on an audio
device that has input streams, even when the app only plays (tccd's log shows a request
with preflight=no). JUCE opens every device through a private aggregate device, which
carries an interface's input streams, so playing to an interface that also has inputs made
macOS ask at the first launch. Here an aggregate of one device used for its output only is
stacked, as a Multi-Output Device is, and has output streams only; with an input device
JUCE builds its usual aggregate.

Delete it once JUCE does this itself: cmake/patches/README.md says what to check at every
JUCE update and how to make the patch again. The lines below keep the CRLF endings of
JUCE's file (.gitattributes).

--- a/modules/juce_audio_devices/native/juce_CoreAudio_mac.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_devices/native/juce_CoreAudio_mac.cpp
@@ -1176,6 +1176,14 @@
 
         addDevice (ioDevices[toUnderlyingType (PlaybackDirection::output)], PlaybackDirection::output);
         addDevice (ioDevices[toUnderlyingType (PlaybackDirection::input)], PlaybackDirection::input);
+
+        // DAW patch (cmake/patches/juce-coreaudio-output-only.patch): one device used for its
+        // output only goes into a stacked aggregate, as in a Multi-Output Device, which has
+        // output streams only. macOS asks for the microphone as soon as an IOProc is created on
+        // a device with input streams (the device itself, a plain aggregate of it, or Apple's
+        // output units alike), long before any input is used.
+        outputOnly = ! ioDevices[toUnderlyingType (PlaybackDirection::input)].isValid()
+                     && devices.getArray().size() == 1;
     }
 
     AggregateAudioDevice createAggregateAudioDevice() const
@@ -1301,6 +1309,7 @@
         description.setString (kAudioAggregateDeviceClockDeviceKey, clockingDeviceUid);
         description.setString (subDeviceKey, clockingDeviceUid);
         description.setInt (kAudioAggregateDeviceIsPrivateKey, ! JUCE_COREAUDIO_LOGGING_ENABLED);
+        description.setInt (kAudioAggregateDeviceIsStackedKey, outputOnly);
         description.setArray (kAudioAggregateDeviceSubDeviceListKey, subDevices);
 
         return description;
@@ -1325,6 +1334,7 @@
 
     String name;
     AudioDevice clockingDevice;
+    bool outputOnly = false;
     UniqueArray<AudioDevice> devices;
     std::array<ChannelMap, 2> channelMap;
 };
